All contract requirements verified correctly. The implementation handles every edge case cited in the contract: signed/fractional/exponent/hex/empty/non-string return null, HTTP-dates require finite `nowMs`, past dates clamp to 0 via `max(0, ...)`, large attempts cap at 300000, and float attempts throw.

The patch is minimal and focused—only the allowed file changed. It correctly fixes all four seeded defects: (1) strict digit-only parsing instead of loose `Number()`, (2) `max(0, ...)` clamping for dates, (3) integer-only attempt validation, and (4) correct `2^(attempt-1)` exponent. Regex constants are clearly named and readable.

